otstrap over seeds, with a fixed resampling seed; \\citealp{Cameron2015APG}). The verdict is obtained by applying a three-way rule to the evaluator's reported interval; the rule is stated by us as the task protocol's reading of the prediction, and its text and the time it was fixed are not retained in the evaluator source or workload manifests, so we make no claim that it was fixed before the evaluation. The prediction ``delay decreases with width'' is \\emph{supported} if the interval lies entirely below zero, \\emph{refuted} if it lies at or above zero, and \\emph{inconclusive} if it straddles zero or the evidence is incomplete. The claim is restricted to the tested setting (modular addition, one training fraction, AdamW with weight decay $1.0$, full batch, one","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
